<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yahya ibn Ali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1035</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Yahya al-Mu'tali</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yahya ibn Ali al-Mu'tali was a Hammudid claimant to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, ruling there in 1021–1023 and 1025–1026. Driven from the capital, he made Málaga his base while still claiming the title of caliph, founding the Hammudid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of Málaga, and was killed in 1035 fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbadid-dynasty">Abbadids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yahya-ibn-ali.jpg" alt="Yahya ibn Ali" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dirham_yahya_22332.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
